fn native_simd_enabled() { return global_get_enable_simd() }

// SIMD feature gates (rolling):
//
// We keep SIMD globally toggleable via `global_get_enable_simd()`, but we also
// gate known-problematic kernels so correctness stays non-negotiable.
//
// Status (2025-12-22):
// - `simd_dot_f32_ptr` is validated by `tests/native/test_simd_suite.oren` for
//   the vector-sized path; tails are handled in Oren wrapper code for now to
//   keep bit-exact semantics (fractional + odd-n guardrails).
// - f32 1x4 / 4x4 higher-level APIs are enabled; the current implementation is
//   built from tail-safe dot kernels (not the direct f32 4x4 microkernel).
fn native_simd_f32_dot_enabled() { return 1 }
fn native_simd_f32_dot4_enabled() { return 1 }

